-- "Within such time as the Court directs": the time is the Court's.  Until the Court directs one the text gives none.
-- src:5447 | 9. Within such time as the Court directs, the company must file in the Registry an affidavit made by the company’s solicitor and an officer of the company competent to make it — ( a )
@ref O 38 r 9 (src:5447-5447)
GIVEN `the date the affidavit was filed in the Registry` IS A DATE
      `the last day fixed by the Court for filing the affidavit` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 9 the affidavit is filed within the time the Court directs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day fixed by the Court for filing the affidavit`
    WHEN JUST fixed THEN
        IF `the date the affidavit was filed in the Registry` AT MOST fixed
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within such time as the Court directs, the company must file in the Registry an affidavit"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the time is "such time as the Court directs" and the Court has directed none

