§§ `Rule 10 -- adjudication of disputed claims`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "If the company contends ..., then, unless the company is willing to secure payment ..., the company must, if the Court so directs,
-- send ... a notice requiring that person": three conditions.  The "unless" is a lifted duty: willing to secure, and the duty is gone.
-- src:5456 | 10. If the company contends that a person is not entitled to be entered in the list of qualifying creditors in respect of any debt or claim or in respect of the full amount claimed by that person in respect of any debt or claim, then, unless the company is willing to secure payment of that debt or claim by appropriating the full amount of the debt or claim, the company must, if the Court so directs, send to that person by post at that person’s last known address a notice requiring that person — ( a )
@ref O 38 r 10 (src:5456-5456)
GIVEN `the company contends that a person is not entitled to be entered in the list of qualifying creditors in respect of any debt or claim or the full amount claimed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is willing to secure payment of that debt or claim by appropriating the full amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court so directs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 10 the duty arises to send the person a notice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the company contends that a person is not entitled to be entered in the list of qualifying creditors in respect of any debt or claim or the full amount claimed` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company contends that a person is not entitled to be entered in the list"
        IF `the company is willing to secure payment of that debt or claim by appropriating the full amount` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the company is willing to secure payment of that debt or claim by appropriating the full amount of the debt or claim"
        IF NOT `the Court so directs` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must, if the Court so directs"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `o 38 r 10 notice to the person` HAS
    `o 38 r 10 it is sent by post` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 38 r 10 it is sent at that person's last known address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 38 r 10(a) it requires that person, within the time specified in the notice, to file an affidavit proving that person's debt or claim or so much of it as is not admitted by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 38 r 10(b) it requires that person to attend the adjudication of that person's debt or claim at the place and time specified in the notice, being the time appointed by the Court` IS A BOOLEAN

