§§ `Rule 12 -- evidence of consent of qualifying creditor`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5479 | 12. The consent of a qualifying creditor to any reduction mentioned in Rule 9( d ) may be proved in such manner as the Court thinks sufficient.
@ref O 38 r 12 (src:5479-5479)
GIVEN `it is the consent of a qualifying creditor to a reduction mentioned in Rule 9(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court thinks the manner of proof sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 12 the consent may be proved in the manner` MEANS
    IF `it is the consent of a qualifying creditor to a reduction mentioned in Rule 9(d)` AND `the Court thinks the manner of proof sufficient`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a "may be proved in such manner as the Court thinks sufficient"; the text does not say that no other manner will do

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 13 -- time, etc., of hearing for confirmation of reduction`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Paragraph (1) is a bar on a date: the hearing "must not be ... before the expiration of at least 8 clear days after the filing of
-- the certificate".  The caller gives the first day on which it may be heard (O 3 r 3: S-T1b).  The twin below, as in every bar, answers
-- JUST FALSE for a hearing on or after that day only as far as this rule goes: the rule grants no hearing.
-- src:5481 | 13. —(1) An originating application for the confirmation of any reduction mentioned in paragraph (2) of Rule 4 must not, where the Court has ordered any proceedings pursuant to that paragraph, be heard before the expiration of at least 8 clear days after the filing of the certificate mentioned in Rule 11. (2) Before the hearing of such an originating application, a notice specifying the day appointed for the hearing must be published at such times and in such newspapers as the Court may direct.
@ref O 38 r 13(1) the period (src:5481-5481)
`o 38 r 13(1) the period after the filing of the certificate before the hearing` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 8
    `period unit` IS `Clear days`
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:5481 | 13. —(1) An originating application for the confirmation of any reduction mentioned in paragraph (2) of Rule 4 must not, where the Court has ordered any proceedings pursuant to that paragraph, be heard before the expiration of at least 8 clear days after the filing of the certificate mentioned in Rule 11. (2) Before the hearing of such an originating application, a notice specifying the day appointed for the hearing must be published at such times and in such newspapers as the Court may direct.
@ref O 38 r 13(1) (src:5481-5481)
GIVEN `the Court has ordered proceedings pursuant to paragraph (2) of Rule 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the hearing` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the first day on which the act may be done` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 13(1) the hearing is barred as too early` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Court has ordered proceedings pursuant to paragraph (2) of Rule 4` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the Court has ordered any proceedings pursuant to that paragraph"
        IF `the date of the hearing` LESS THAN `o 3 r 3 the first day on which the act may be done` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not ... be heard before the expiration of at least 8 clear days after the filing of the certificate"

-- src:5481 | 13. —(1) An originating application for the confirmation of any reduction mentioned in paragraph (2) of Rule 4 must not, where the Court has ordered any proceedings pursuant to that paragraph, be heard before the expiration of at least 8 clear days after the filing of the certificate mentioned in Rule 11. (2) Before the hearing of such an originating application, a notice specifying the day appointed for the hearing must be published at such times and in such newspapers as the Court may direct.
@ref O 38 r 13(2) (src:5481-5481)
GIVEN `it is an originating application of the kind mentioned in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice was published` IS A DATE
      `the date of the hearing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 13(2) the notice is published before the hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is an originating application of the kind mentioned in paragraph (1)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such an originating application"
        IF `the date the notice was published` LESS THAN `the date of the hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before the hearing of such an originating application, a notice specifying the day appointed for the hearing must be published"

DECLARE `o 38 r 13(2) notice of the hearing` HAS
    `o 38 r 13(2) it specifies the day appointed for the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 38 r 13(2) it is published at such times and in such newspapers as the Court may direct` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:5481 | 13. —(1) An originating application for the confirmation of any reduction mentioned in paragraph (2) of Rule 4 must not, where the Court has ordered any proceedings pursuant to that paragraph, be heard before the expiration of at least 8 clear days after the filing of the certificate mentioned in Rule 11. (2) Before the hearing of such an originating application, a notice specifying the day appointed for the hearing must be published at such times and in such newspapers as the Court may direct.
@ref O 38 r 13(2) (src:5481-5481)
GIVEN notice IS AN `o 38 r 13(2) notice of the hearing`
      `it is an originating application of the kind mentioned in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 13(2) the notice states and is published as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is an originating application of the kind mentioned in paragraph (1)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): `it is an originating application of the kind mentioned in paragraph (1)` does not hold, so paragraph (2) does not apply
        IF NOT notice's `o 38 r 13(2) it specifies the day appointed for the hearing` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2) is a bare "must be published"; the text does not say what follows (O 3 r 2(4), outside this range, lists what the Court may do)
        IF NOT notice's `o 38 r 13(2) it is published at such times and in such newspapers as the Court may direct` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2) is a bare "must be published"; the text does not say what follows
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 14 -- applications under section 148`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Paragraph (1) counts BACKWARDS: "at least 28 days before the date fixed for the hearing".  The caller gives the last day for
-- service (O 3 r 3); the function compares.  The trustee limb is owed only if the trustee is not the Official Assignee.
-- src:5483 | 14. —(1) A bankrupt who intends to make an application for permission to act as director, or to take part in or be concerned in the management, of a corporation under section 148, must serve a copy each of the application and the affidavit supporting the application at least 28 days before the date fixed for the hearing upon — ( a )
-- src:5484 | the Official Assignee; and
-- src:5485 | ( b )
-- src:5486 | the trustee of the bankrupt’s estate, if not the Official Assignee.
@ref O 38 r 14(1) (src:5483-5486)
GIVEN `the person is a bankrupt who intends to make an application under section 148` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 14(1) the duty arises to serve a copy of the application and the affidavit` MEANS
    IF `the person is a bankrupt who intends to make an application under section 148`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A bankrupt who intends to make an application for permission to act as director, or to take part in or be concerned in the management, of a corporation under section 148, must"

-- src:5483 | 14. —(1) A bankrupt who intends to make an application for permission to act as director, or to take part in or be concerned in the management, of a corporation under section 148, must serve a copy each of the application and the affidavit supporting the application at least 28 days before the date fixed for the hearing upon — ( a )
@ref O 38 r 14(1) the period (src:5483-5483)
`o 38 r 14(1) the period before the hearing for serving` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 28
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `Before the anchor`
-- src:5483 | 14. —(1) A bankrupt who intends to make an application for permission to act as director, or to take part in or be concerned in the management, of a corporation under section 148, must serve a copy each of the application and the affidavit supporting the application at least 28 days before the date fixed for the hearing upon — ( a )
-- src:5484 | the Official Assignee; and
-- src:5485 | ( b )
-- src:5486 | the trustee of the bankrupt’s estate, if not the Official Assignee.
@ref O 38 r 14(1) (src:5483-5486)
GIVEN `the person is a bankrupt who intends to make an application under section 148` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date a copy was served on the Official Assignee` IS A DATE
      `the trustee of the bankrupt's estate is not the Official Assignee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date a copy was served on the trustee` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 14(1) the copies are served at least 28 days before the hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is a bankrupt who intends to make an application under section 148` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise; see `o 38 r 14(1) the duty arises to serve a copy of the application and the affidavit`
        IF `the date a copy was served on the Official Assignee` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` AND ((NOT `the trustee of the bankrupt's estate is not the Official Assignee`) OR `the date a copy was served on the trustee` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must serve a copy each of the application and the affidavit supporting the application at least 28 days before the date fixed for the hearing"

DECLARE `o 38 r 14(2) affidavit` HAS
    `o 38 r 14(2)(a) it states the name and registration number of the corporation in question` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 38 r 14(2)(b) it states the nature of the business or intended business of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 38 r 14(2)(c) it states the place or places where the business of the corporation is to be carried on` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 38 r 14(2)(d) it states whether the corporation is to be incorporated as a private or public company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 38 r 14(2)(e) it states the persons who are, or are to be, principally responsible for conducting the affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 38 r 14(2)(f) it states the manner and capacity in which the bankrupt proposes to take part in or be concerned in the management of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 38 r 14(2)(g) it states the emoluments or other benefits to be obtained by the bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:5487 | (2) An affidavit mentioned in paragraph (1) must state the following particulars: ( a )
-- src:5488 | the name and registration number of the corporation in question;
-- src:5489 | ( b )
-- src:5490 | the nature of the business or intended business of the corporation;
-- src:5491 | ( c )
-- src:5492 | the place or places where the business of the corporation is to be carried on;
-- src:5493 | ( d )
-- src:5494 | in the case of a corporation that is not yet incorporated — whether it is to be incorporated as a private or public company;
-- src:5495 | ( e )
-- src:5496 | the persons who are, or are to be, principally responsible for conducting the affairs of the corporation, whether as directors, managers or otherwise;
-- src:5497 | ( f )
-- src:5498 | the manner and capacity in which the bankrupt proposes to take part in or be concerned in the management of the corporation;
-- src:5499 | ( g )
-- src:5500 | the emoluments or other benefits to be obtained by the bankrupt by acting as director of the corporation or for taking part in the management of the business of the corporation, as the case may be.
@ref O 38 r 14(2) (src:5487-5500)
GIVEN affidavit IS AN `o 38 r 14(2) affidavit`
      `the corporation is not yet incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 14(2) the affidavit states the particulars the paragraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT affidavit's `o 38 r 14(2)(a) it states the name and registration number of the corporation in question` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2) is a bare "must state the following particulars"; the text does not say what follows (O 3 r 2(4), outside this range, lists what the Court may do)
        IF NOT affidavit's `o 38 r 14(2)(b) it states the nature of the business or intended business of the corporation` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2) is a bare "must state the following particulars"; the text does not say what follows
        IF NOT affidavit's `o 38 r 14(2)(c) it states the place or places where the business of the corporation is to be carried on` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2) is a bare "must state the following particulars"; the text does not say what follows
        IF `the corporation is not yet incorporated` AND (NOT affidavit's `o 38 r 14(2)(d) it states whether the corporation is to be incorporated as a private or public company`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2) is a bare "must state the following particulars"; the text does not say what follows; owed only where `the corporation is not yet incorporated`
        IF NOT affidavit's `o 38 r 14(2)(e) it states the persons who are, or are to be, principally responsible for conducting the affairs of the corporation` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2) is a bare "must state the following particulars"; the text does not say what follows
        IF NOT affidavit's `o 38 r 14(2)(f) it states the manner and capacity in which the bankrupt proposes to take part in or be concerned in the management of the corporation` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2) is a bare "must state the following particulars"; the text does not say what follows
        IF NOT affidavit's `o 38 r 14(2)(g) it states the emoluments or other benefits to be obtained by the bankrupt` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2) is a bare "must state the following particulars"; the text does not say what follows
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
-- src:5501 | (3) The trustee of the bankrupt’s estate must — ( a )
-- src:5502 | make a report to the Court at least 14 days before the date fixed for the hearing; and
-- src:5503 | ( b )
-- src:5504 | serve a copy of the report on the bankrupt as soon as practicable after it is made.
@ref O 38 r 14(3) (src:5501-5504)
GIVEN `the bankrupt has made an application under section 148` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 14(3) the duty arises on the trustee to make a report and serve a copy` MEANS
    IF `the bankrupt has made an application under section 148`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The trustee of the bankrupt's estate must" make a report in connection with an application under section 148

-- src:5501 | (3) The trustee of the bankrupt’s estate must — ( a )
-- src:5502 | make a report to the Court at least 14 days before the date fixed for the hearing; and
@ref O 38 r 14(3)(a) the period (src:5501-5502)
`o 38 r 14(3)(a) the period before the hearing for making the report` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `Before the anchor`
-- src:5501 | (3) The trustee of the bankrupt’s estate must — ( a )
-- src:5502 | make a report to the Court at least 14 days before the date fixed for the hearing; and
@ref O 38 r 14(3)(a) (src:5501-5502)
GIVEN `the bankrupt has made an application under section 148` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the report was made to the Court` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 14(3)(a) the report is made at least 14 days before the hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the bankrupt has made an application under section 148` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise
        IF `the date the report was made to the Court` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "make a report to the Court at least 14 days before the date fixed for the hearing"
-- src:5503 | ( b )
-- src:5504 | serve a copy of the report on the bankrupt as soon as practicable after it is made.
@ref O 38 r 14(3)(b) (src:5503-5504)
GIVEN `the bankrupt has made an application under section 148` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the report was served on the bankrupt as soon as practicable after it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 14(3)(b) the copy of the report is served on the bankrupt as soon as practicable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the bankrupt has made an application under section 148` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise; see `o 38 r 14(3) the duty arises on the trustee to make a report and serve a copy`
        IF `a copy of the report was served on the bankrupt as soon as practicable after it was made` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "as soon as practicable" is a standard the text does not turn into a number of days

-- Paragraph (4): the definitions.
-- src:5505 | (4) In this Rule — “bankrupt” means — ( a )
-- src:5506 | an individual debtor who has been adjudged bankrupt by a bankruptcy order made under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 or previous written law; or
-- src:5507 | ( b )
-- src:5508 | a partner in a firm against which a bankruptcy order has been made under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 or previous written law;
@ref O 38 r 14(4) “bankrupt” (src:5505-5508)
GIVEN `the person is an individual debtor who has been adjudged bankrupt by a bankruptcy order made under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 or previous written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partner in a firm against which a bankruptcy order has been made under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 or previous written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 14(4) the person is a bankrupt for this Rule` MEANS
    IF `the person is an individual debtor who has been adjudged bankrupt by a bankruptcy order made under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 or previous written law` OR `the person is a partner in a firm against which a bankruptcy order has been made under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 or previous written law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“bankrupt” means — (a) an individual debtor who has been adjudged bankrupt ...; or (b) a partner in a firm against which a bankruptcy order has been made"

-- src:5509 | “Official Assignee” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018;
@ref O 38 r 14(4) “Official Assignee” (src:5509-5509)
GIVEN `irda 2018 s 2(1) the person is the Official Assignee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 14(4) Official Assignee has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` MEANS
    CONSIDER `irda 2018 s 2(1) the person is the Official Assignee`
    WHEN JUST answer THEN JUST answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018", which is not among the sources

-- src:5510 | “trustee”, in relation to a bankrupt, means the trustee of the bankrupt’s estate and includes the Official Assignee when acting as trustee of the bankrupt’s estate.
@ref O 38 r 14(4) “trustee” (src:5510-5510)
GIVEN `the person is the trustee of the bankrupt's estate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Official Assignee acting as trustee of the bankrupt's estate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 14(4) the person is a trustee in relation to the bankrupt` MEANS
    IF `the person is the trustee of the bankrupt's estate` OR `the person is the Official Assignee acting as trustee of the bankrupt's estate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“trustee”, in relation to a bankrupt, means the trustee of the bankrupt's estate and includes the Official Assignee when acting as trustee of the bankrupt's estate"

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 38 -- the same duties as regulative rules`
-- ===========================================================================

-- The text names no consequence of a late act, so a late act is a BREACH only in the sense that the period has run
-- (O 3 r 2(4), outside this range, lists what the Court may do).  Days are a plain count; the count the Rules require
-- is O 3 r 3 (see the decision functions).  Two duties are not given here: the duties counted backwards from a hearing
-- (r 14(1), r 14(3)(a)), which a WITHIN clause cannot express, and the duty whose time is the Court's (r 9).

DECLARE `o 38 party under Order 38` IS ONE OF
    `o 38 r 5(1) the company`

DECLARE `o 38 act under Order 38` IS ONE OF
    `o 38 r 5(1) file the affidavit in the Registry`
    `o 38 r 5(3) leave the list at the Registry`
    `o 38 r 7 send the notice by post`

-- src:5418 | 5. —(1) Where under Rule 4 the Court orders proceedings mentioned in paragraph (2) of that Rule, the company in question must, within 14 days after the making of the order, file in the Registry an affidavit made by an officer of the company competent to make it verifying a list containing — ( a )
@ref O 38 r 5(1) (src:5418-5418)
GIVEN `the Court orders under Rule 4 the proceedings mentioned in paragraph (2) of that Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
`o 38 r 5(1) the duty to file the affidavit` MEANS
    IF `the Court orders under Rule 4 the proceedings mentioned in paragraph (2) of that Rule`
    THEN PARTY `o 38 r 5(1) the company`
         MUST `o 38 r 5(1) file the affidavit in the Registry`
         WITHIN (`o 38 r 5(1) the period for filing the affidavit`'s `period length`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `o 38 r 5(1) the company` BECAUSE "the affidavit was not filed within 14 days after the making of the order"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:5425 | (3) The list of qualifying creditors must be left at the Registry not later than one day after the affidavit is filed.
@ref O 38 r 5(3) (src:5425-5425)
`o 38 r 5(3) the duty to leave the list at the Registry` MEANS
    PARTY `o 38 r 5(1) the company`
    MUST `o 38 r 5(3) leave the list at the Registry`
    WITHIN (`o 38 r 5(3) the period for leaving the list at the Registry`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 38 r 5(1) the company` BECAUSE "the list was not left at the Registry within one day after the affidavit was filed"

-- src:5429 | 7. Within 14 days after filing the affidavit required by Rule 5, the company must send by post to each qualifying creditor named in the list of qualifying creditors exhibited to the affidavit, at the qualifying creditor’s last known address, a notice stating — ( a )
@ref O 38 r 7 (src:5429-5429)
`o 38 r 7 the duty to send the notice` MEANS
    PARTY `o 38 r 5(1) the company`
    MUST `o 38 r 7 send the notice by post`
    WITHIN (`o 38 r 7 the period for sending the notice`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 38 r 5(1) the company` BECAUSE "the notice was not sent within 14 days after the affidavit was filed"
